   ],
   "html": "<p><strong>Supergirl </strong>arrived with a message of her own, creating a media moment around her introduction and taking over the Artspace at The Public Hotel in NYC to debut the trailer. Surrounded by a themed atmosphere and programming, we showcased the out-of-this-world intergalactic adventure that is <em>Supergirl.</em></p>\n<p>Hosted by <strong>James Gunn</strong>, <strong>Milly Alcock</strong>, and <strong>Craig Gilespie</strong>, the night offered an exclusive first look at the latest release from DC Studios, but done in a way to set the stage for her era.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "atmosphere & Decor",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "html": "<p>Guests entered through branded glowing red rubber curtains, flowing into a neon stairwell highlighted by Supergirl's emblem on reflective mirrored walls. The space was styled with throw pillows, acrylic emblem centerpieces, and a blue Krypto dog bowl, offering a charming nod to the beloved sidekick. A title treatment photo wall featured a cosmic-blue backdrop with splatter texture, a 3D logo, and striking blue-and-red pulsing LED tube lights.</p>"
    },
